1
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:52,990
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:56,020
[Episode 4]

3
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:01,650
Liu Juan, a police officer
at Yuhong Square Police Station,

4
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:03,500
brought a child to the office

5
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,140
for an overnight stay during her shift.

6
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:07,510
For that, she is given
a disciplinary warning

7
00:01:08,070 --> 00:01:11,039
and disqualified from the this year's
Outstanding Police Officer

8
00:01:11,350 --> 00:01:12,510
selection.

9
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:24,120
This is

10
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,289
the di-division's decision.

11
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:29,680
That child isn't even mine.

12
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:31,200
Why am I being punished?

13
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:33,430
I gave an explanation on your behalf,

14
00:01:33,430 --> 00:01:34,479
but the higher-ups said

15
00:01:34,479 --> 00:01:36,570
that since you are the child's
temporary guardian,

16
00:01:36,570 --> 00:01:38,280
looking after her
is a personal matter of yours.

17
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,210
Did I ask to be her temporary guardian?

18
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:42,039
If I were out on patrol,

19
00:01:42,039 --> 00:01:43,350
saw an unattended child,

20
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:44,500
and brought them back,

21
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:45,640
would I be punished?

22
00:01:58,979 --> 00:01:59,700
What's with you?

23
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:00,700
Nothing. I just...

24
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:04,540
Have some water.

25
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:05,450
T-Take a sip.

26
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:09,900
Just an old ailment.

27
00:02:10,610 --> 00:02:11,560
-Look at you.
-Any loud noise

28
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,130
makes my head start pounding.

29
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,690
It's okay. I'll be fine
after a short rest.

30
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:17,930
See, what a mess.

31
00:02:17,930 --> 00:02:18,690
How about...

32
00:02:19,810 --> 00:02:20,930
you get back to your work?

33
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:23,250
Go do your thing.

34
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,030
I'll get going then.

35
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:29,060
What should be done about this, huh?

36
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,420
[Vitamin C]

37
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,320
Complete shambles.

38
00:02:52,970 --> 00:02:53,840
Sit somewhere else.

39
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:55,560
Stop hogging my seat and scribbling.

40
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,300
This is you.

41
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:59,190
This is me.

42
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:00,590
This is a snowman.

43
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:01,680
What's that about now?

44
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,340
All that mumbling,

45
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:03,780
and I didn't understand a word.

46
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:07,530
This is you.

47
00:03:08,210 --> 00:03:09,530
Who's this? Me?

48
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:13,120
And what's this thing?

49
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:14,460
A snowman?

50
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:17,970
You're a little girl from the south.

51
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:19,250
Have you even seen a snowman?

52
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:22,020
She's actually a good painter.

53
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,120
It's all over.

54
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,860
My transfer to the division fell through.

55
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:33,310
I won't get a pay raise either.

56
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:35,360
When will I ever save enough money

57
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,710
for my younger brother's wedding?

58
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,690
Come on. I'm taking you out.

59
00:04:06,210 --> 00:04:06,750
Hurry. Quick.

60
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:08,130
Get up already.

61
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:10,380
Or you'll be late for work.

62
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,090
Get a move on.

63
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:12,890
Sure.

64
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:13,770
Okay.

65
00:04:25,790 --> 00:04:26,730
He had too...

66
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,880
too much to drink last night, huh?

67
00:04:32,690 --> 00:04:33,420
Going out, aren't you?

68
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,600
How about I give you a ride?

69
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:51,980
This motorcycle.

70
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,600
The smaller key's for the lock.

71
00:05:14,810 --> 00:05:15,780
Hand me the lock.

72
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:37,130
Hold the throttle grip

73
00:05:37,130 --> 00:05:39,000
as you step on that lever.

74
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,980
-This lever?
-Step on it. Yes, that's the one.

75
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:41,860
Both actions at once.

76
00:05:44,390 --> 00:05:45,290
Simultaneously.

77
00:06:09,810 --> 00:06:10,580
Get on.

78
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,510
Hold on tight.

79
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,310
Chief,

80
00:06:32,310 --> 00:06:33,710
you must give me an explanation today.

81
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,690
That man froze to death.

82
00:06:34,690 --> 00:06:35,630
Why am I being punished?

83
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:36,720
Did I have the wind blow,

84
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:37,659
or did I make it snow?

85
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:46,260
This is nothing personal against you.

86
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,570
The division meant

87
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:49,500
for this decision as a warning.

88
00:06:49,870 --> 00:06:51,250
Any officer would've been
treated the same.

89
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:52,310
How is it nothing personal against me?

90
00:06:52,310 --> 00:06:53,950
The notice has made it perfectly clear:

91
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:55,450
a disciplinary warning to me
for looking after

92
00:06:55,450 --> 00:06:56,740
a child while I was on duty.

93
00:06:56,740 --> 00:06:57,440
Look at her.

94
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,600
Look at her little face.

95
00:06:58,980 --> 00:07:00,370
How could she possibly be my child?

96
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,950
See, she has a round face,
while mine is long.

97
00:07:02,950 --> 00:07:05,160
She's got prominent double eyelids,
while mine are hidden.

98
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:07,770
She has a rounded nose tip,
while I have a flat nose bridge.

99
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:08,480
You...

100
00:07:10,190 --> 00:07:11,810
Why is it so cold in your office?

101
00:07:12,010 --> 00:07:13,770
The kid is catching a cold.

102
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:16,130
The division is tight on funds.

103
00:07:16,130 --> 00:07:17,630
Blow your nose. Blow hard.

104
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:33,870
Sun Zheng is a real bastard.

105
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,480
After we divorced so many years ago,

106
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:37,540
he dumped the child of his mistress
here with me

107
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:38,420
without a single word.

108
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:40,400
Did I cross or mess with anyone?

109
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:42,240
This girl is not my daughter.

110
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,650
But I couldn't have left her alone

111
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,420
on the streets
and let her freeze to death, right?

112
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:46,680
Even stray cats and dogs

113
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:47,310
shouldn't be ignored

114
00:07:47,310 --> 00:07:48,420
in such cold weather.

115
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:50,070
I didn't bend the rules
for personal ends, did I?

116
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:51,950
I was obviously doing a good deed.

117
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:54,680
Besides...

118
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:56,930
I was on the night shift,

119
00:07:56,930 --> 00:07:58,240
and I kept her at the station.

120
00:07:58,570 --> 00:08:00,100
It didn't get in the way of my patrol.

121
00:08:00,510 --> 00:08:02,160
I was supposed to patrol every two hours.

122
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:04,240
Zhao Changyou froze to death at 10:00,

123
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:04,980
right?

124
00:08:05,250 --> 00:08:06,510
When I was patrolling and spotted him

125
00:08:06,510 --> 00:08:07,000
at 11:00,

126
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,430
he had already turned into a block of ice.

127
00:08:08,630 --> 00:08:09,420
Even doctors who work miracles

128
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:10,060
couldn't have helped

129
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:11,300
and brought him back to life.

130
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,460
Why issue a public criticism against me?

131
00:08:13,630 --> 00:08:14,620
Don't get all worked up.

132
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:15,830
I'm not worked up.

133
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:17,600
I just feel wronged.

134
00:08:20,870 --> 00:08:21,660
Look,

135
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:23,820
I'm a woman of a certain age,
single and divorced.

136
00:08:24,070 --> 00:08:25,690
This four-year-old kid coming

137
00:08:25,950 --> 00:08:27,570
from nowhere isn't even related to me,

138
00:08:27,570 --> 00:08:29,500
yet she just became a burden
on my shoulders.

139
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:32,700
B-But instead of helping me out
and taking care

140
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,580
of the child, the station made me

141
00:08:34,789 --> 00:08:37,000
take the blame when trouble occurred.

142
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:38,840
Is there any sense of human decency

143
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,080
or class solidarity?

144
00:08:42,780 --> 00:08:43,970
Besides, this kid

145
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,530
has no family here.

146
00:08:45,530 --> 00:08:46,460
Whenever she opens

147
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:47,670
her mouth,

148
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,700
it's total gibberish.

149
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:53,050
Hello, I'm Qianqian.

150
00:08:53,050 --> 00:08:55,530
I'm four years old.

151
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:58,010
Did you hear that?

152
00:08:58,010 --> 00:08:59,010
Sh-She speaks Cantonese.

153
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:00,580
D-Do you understand a word of it?

154
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:01,860
Look at her.

155
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:03,170
What will happen if she gets sick

156
00:09:03,170 --> 00:09:04,370
when nobody is around?

157
00:09:04,370 --> 00:09:05,910
How's that going to work?
Who should be responsible?

158
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,670
Chief, if you really think

159
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:08,770
that I handled personal matters

160
00:09:08,770 --> 00:09:10,080
during work hours,

161
00:09:10,270 --> 00:09:11,100
how about this—

162
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:12,460
from today on, whenever I'm on duty,

163
00:09:13,150 --> 00:09:14,170
I'll send the child

164
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:15,860
to your place.

165
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:17,130
Just ask your wife

166
00:09:17,270 --> 00:09:18,720
to look after her for a while, okay?

167
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:26,910
Juan,

168
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,920
the division has treated you well
over these years, right?

169
00:09:32,110 --> 00:09:33,250
Years ago, you went to Guangzhou

170
00:09:33,250 --> 00:09:34,500
and caused a huge mess there.

171
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:37,120
I personally talked
with the local police station,

172
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:38,250
so they let you off.

173
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:40,530
When that incident of yours was reported

174
00:09:40,550 --> 00:09:44,220
to the municipal bureau, every division
officer put in a good word for you.

175
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:46,940
Only by being transferred
from the division to this station

176
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:48,340
did you manage to keep your job.

177
00:09:49,390 --> 00:09:50,320
You remember it, don't you?

178
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:52,510
What are you trying to say?

179
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,100
As you know,

180
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:58,150
since the restructuring

181
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:00,410
of state-owned enterprises
in Tiecheng started,

182
00:10:00,770 --> 00:10:02,410
there have been waves of laid-off workers.

183
00:10:02,770 --> 00:10:04,940
Every division and station in the city

184
00:10:05,270 --> 00:10:07,170
is walking on eggshells,

185
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:08,910
fearing what may happen.

186
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:10,890
You guys were just unlucky.

187
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,510
A man died a hundred meters
away from your station.

188
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:15,860
If his family makes a big fuss over it,

189
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:17,030
not only your station,

190
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,650
but also the entire division will suffer.

191
00:10:19,650 --> 00:10:22,170
This public criticism
isn't a reprimand aimed at you.

192
00:10:22,170 --> 00:10:23,720
It's only to pacify
the family of the deceased.

193
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,320
Well then...

194
00:10:24,630 --> 00:10:26,750
It's just a minor public criticism.

195
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:27,860
An administrative penalty

196
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:29,100
won't affect your promotion.

197
00:10:30,650 --> 00:10:32,770
Juan, you're a veteran officer.

198
00:10:33,410 --> 00:10:35,550
Just take the blame for the division
this time.

199
00:10:35,890 --> 00:10:37,080
Consider it a way to return the favor,

200
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:38,270
okay?

201
00:10:40,670 --> 00:10:42,010
Will it really not affect my promotion?

202
00:10:42,010 --> 00:10:43,100
Absolutely not.

203
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:45,120
Then when will I be transferred back?

204
00:10:49,050 --> 00:10:49,840
Well, um...

205
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:51,030
I need to use the restroom now.

206
00:10:51,030 --> 00:10:53,120
I'm getting old. Can't hold it in.

207
00:10:55,010 --> 00:10:56,250
What an adorable little girl.

208
00:11:02,290 --> 00:11:04,150
[Office for Political Affairs]

209
00:11:03,570 --> 00:11:04,520
Are you feeling cold?

210
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,920
Look, your nose has been running all day.

211
00:11:09,150 --> 00:11:09,840
Blow harder.

212
00:11:15,150 --> 00:11:16,150
The phone is ringing.

213
00:11:16,150 --> 00:11:17,910
Is your hat too light for winter?

214
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:21,140
What is it that's so urgent?

215
00:11:22,370 --> 00:11:23,290
Should I answer the phone?

216
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:25,820
I should?

217
00:11:26,750 --> 00:11:27,650
This is your idea.

218
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,270
I'll answer it then.

219
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:35,890
Hello.

220
00:11:36,050 --> 00:11:37,240
Is Chief Zhang there?

221
00:11:37,770 --> 00:11:38,780
He's gone to the restroom,

222
00:11:39,010 --> 00:11:40,340
saying that he's getting old
and can't hold it in.

223
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:41,410
Tell me if anything has come up.

224
00:11:41,410 --> 00:11:42,460
I'll pass the message to him.

225
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:45,960
I'm He Liang from the Second CIU
of the Yingjin Municipal Bureau.

226
00:11:46,150 --> 00:11:48,290
We've been working on a case of smuggling

227
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,840
wildlife products for over six months.

228
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,500
Recently, we just got a lead

229
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,640
and tracked down one of the suspects.

230
00:11:53,660 --> 00:11:54,750
He lives in your jurisdiction.

231
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:57,410
So we'd like to ask for
your division's help

232
00:11:57,410 --> 00:11:58,710
to get this person under control.

233
00:11:58,890 --> 00:11:59,740
We'll arrive shortly.

234
00:11:59,810 --> 00:12:01,740
Okay. Just give me

235
00:12:01,770 --> 00:12:02,960
the name and address

236
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,390
of the suspect.

237
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,270
The name is Zhao Changyou.

238
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:08,050
As for the address... Let me check.

239
00:12:08,910 --> 00:12:09,820
No need for that.

240
00:12:10,390 --> 00:12:11,480
I know where he is.

241
00:12:11,950 --> 00:12:12,830
Really?

242
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:15,280
Could you have him under control now?

243
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:17,190
Not a problem. You just come over.

244
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:19,220
This man's completely under control now.

245
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:21,460
Come straight to our place
after you get off the train.

246
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,690
You'll be just in time
to see his body thaw.

247
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,220
Listen, shortly after

248
00:12:36,950 --> 00:12:38,370
Zhao Changyou froze to death,

249
00:12:38,610 --> 00:12:39,940
the police came looking for him.

250
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:41,630
Suspicious, isn't it?

251
00:12:46,130 --> 00:12:48,220
I thought he was just a drunkard.

252
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:51,910
Who would've known he was also
a suspect in a smuggling case?

253
00:12:54,770 --> 00:12:57,880
Then he probably didn't freeze to death.

254
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,360
Suppose he was murdered

255
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,070
and dumped in the stadium,

256
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,010
then I would be off the hook,

257
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:09,100
right?

258
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:18,460
Let's go.

259
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:19,500
Stand up.

260
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:22,630
Time to get to work

261
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:23,940
and find clues.

262
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:25,360
You're so heavy.

263
00:13:29,410 --> 00:13:30,410
Mind your steps.

264
00:13:37,170 --> 00:13:38,460
Keep this in mind:

265
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:39,320
in this world,

266
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:41,390
there's no such thing as a ghost or god.

267
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,030
Living people are the scary ones.

268
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,340
What's to fear about the dead?

269
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:45,270
Think about it.

270
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:47,620
If a dead person really became a ghost,

271
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:48,770
decided to scare you,

272
00:13:48,770 --> 00:13:49,820
and frightened you to death,

273
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:51,860
then you would turn into a ghost yourself.

274
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:52,750
Both ending up in the same place,

275
00:13:52,750 --> 00:13:54,150
you would get to beat him up. Understood?

276
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,820
So don't be afraid when we're in there.

277
00:13:57,820 --> 00:13:59,150
Just stand next to me. Alright?

278
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:02,940
[Police Badge]

279
00:14:01,890 --> 00:14:03,100
This represents righteousness.

280
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:04,240
Keep it with you.

281
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:05,320
All spirits will be deterred.

282
00:14:05,630 --> 00:14:06,130
Let's go.

283
00:14:11,290 --> 00:14:13,290
[Specimen name: Meningeal tissue]

284
00:14:13,010 --> 00:14:15,130
The kid has some real guts.

285
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,510
She probably

286
00:14:16,510 --> 00:14:18,030
has no idea what's in that jar.

287
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:22,840
She knows, obviously.

288
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:25,340
Then she may
attend medical school and get in

289
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:26,320
the same profession as you.

290
00:14:26,910 --> 00:14:27,600
Sounds viable.

291
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:28,480
I'm telling you,

292
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,340
she must have a certain gift

293
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:30,340
since she's not afraid at all.

294
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,980
What did the autopsy reveal?

295
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:34,860
Before this man froze to death,

296
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,510
he had quite a meal.

297
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:38,240
What did he eat?

298
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:40,790
From his stomach,

299
00:14:40,890 --> 00:14:42,150
we found undigested

300
00:14:42,150 --> 00:14:43,390
bean sprouts, cabbage, peanuts,

301
00:14:44,010 --> 00:14:45,370
jellyfish with scallions,
twice-cooked pork,

302
00:14:45,650 --> 00:14:46,750
and dumplings
filled with pickled cabbage.

303
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:49,250
This means he had just enjoyed a big meal.

304
00:14:49,390 --> 00:14:50,940
He probably ate near the square.

305
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:51,800
I have an inquiry.

306
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,180
I'm from Yuhong Police Station.

307
00:14:53,390 --> 00:14:54,790
Have you seen this man?

308
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:55,630
No, never.

309
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:56,770
Have you seen this man?

310
00:14:57,270 --> 00:14:58,220
No.

311
00:14:58,220 --> 00:14:59,510
Take a look at it too, please.

312
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:00,790
Does he seem familiar to you?

313
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:02,720
No, we've never seen this guy.

314
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:03,600
In addition,

315
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,170
his blood alcohol level

316
00:15:05,170 --> 00:15:06,750
was insanely high.

317
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,980
He must have drunk
at least two catties of liquor.

318
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:12,460
Then he definitely didn't eat alone.

319
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:15,180
[Yuhong Stadium] [Funeral Store]
[Yuhong Subdistrict]

320
00:15:13,150 --> 00:15:14,120
I remember

321
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:16,000
when I found him,

322
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:16,980
there was a cigarette in his mouth.

323
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:19,530
But on his body,

324
00:15:19,530 --> 00:15:22,200
we didn't find cigarette cases, lighters,
or matches.

325
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,370
None of those.

326
00:15:23,150 --> 00:15:26,150
[Gang's Diner]
[Please head to the second floor]

327
00:15:23,870 --> 00:15:25,030
That means there was

328
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,240
someone else at the scene.

329
00:15:27,150 --> 00:15:28,150
You busy?

330
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:29,910
Hello.

331
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:31,870
I'm an officer of Yuhong Police Station.

332
00:15:32,130 --> 00:15:33,240
I'd like to ask you about someone.

333
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:34,470
Have you seen this person?

334
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:41,780
He looks a bit familiar.

335
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:43,740
Really?

336
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:44,470
Yes.

337
00:15:44,630 --> 00:15:45,140
I recall it.

338
00:15:45,290 --> 00:15:46,780
This man ate here a few days ago.

339
00:15:47,270 --> 00:15:47,980
Did he really?

340
00:15:48,550 --> 00:15:49,860
He absolutely did.

341
00:15:50,170 --> 00:15:51,530
This little diner of mine

342
00:15:51,530 --> 00:15:53,000
usually receives

343
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,720
taxi drivers, delivery guys, and such.

344
00:15:55,030 --> 00:15:57,360
In most cases, they just order
rice with toppings or fried noodles.

345
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,250
Those are highly affordable.

346
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,670
But that day, this man
and his fellow ordered...

347
00:16:01,890 --> 00:16:02,740
several dishes, anyway.

348
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:04,270
I got so busy with that.

349
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:05,480
Jellyfish ran out,

350
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:06,870
so I had to get some from Si next door.

351
00:16:07,530 --> 00:16:09,750
His fellow? So this man wasn't here alone?

352
00:16:09,750 --> 00:16:10,790
There was another man.

353
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:11,790
He was quite tall

354
00:16:12,150 --> 00:16:12,840
and slender,

355
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:14,270
with a moustache.

356
00:16:14,270 --> 00:16:15,650
Looked like he was

357
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:16,550
in his twenties,

358
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,250
or maybe thirties.

359
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,530
How old exactly?

360
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:21,100
Twenty to thirty.

361
00:16:21,910 --> 00:16:22,650
Did they drink?

362
00:16:22,910 --> 00:16:23,580
Oh my.

363
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:25,030
The two of them drank a lot.

364
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:26,460
How much exactly?

365
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:28,340
Just a lot.

366
00:16:30,910 --> 00:16:31,790
When did they leave?

367
00:16:32,610 --> 00:16:33,360
Late at night.

368
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:34,850
How come you just

369
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:36,560
can't give me a straight answer?

370
00:16:36,650 --> 00:16:37,500
Oh, come on.

371
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:39,550
H-How could I be sure
about so many details?

372
00:16:39,550 --> 00:16:41,030
I'm the only staffer in this diner.

373
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,130
I have to do everything—

374
00:16:42,130 --> 00:16:44,030
washing, cooking, chopping, and cleaning.

375
00:16:44,030 --> 00:16:45,670
How am I supposed to keep track
of every customer?

376
00:16:47,370 --> 00:16:48,510
Did they leave together?

377
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:49,890
Probably.

378
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:52,080
What did I...

379
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:53,720
What did I tell you?

380
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:54,890
Stop it.

381
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:56,390
I did the investigation myself.

382
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:56,750
Fine.

383
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:58,220
What does it have to do
with the Yellow and the Green Immortal?

384
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:04,069
Who do you think this person is?

385
00:17:04,589 --> 00:17:06,530
I've asked around in the neighborhood.

386
00:17:07,310 --> 00:17:09,460
Only this diner owner said
he had seen him.

387
00:17:10,069 --> 00:17:10,770
But...

388
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,880
he couldn't describe
this man's looks accurately.

389
00:17:13,089 --> 00:17:14,270
Everything's so vague.

390
00:17:15,349 --> 00:17:17,660
No first name. No last name.

391
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,380
How am I supposed to find him out?

392
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:30,160
May I speak my opinion?

393
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:32,010
Just go ahead
and say whatever you have to say.

394
00:17:33,050 --> 00:17:34,290
Didn't you tell me to stop?

395
00:17:34,290 --> 00:17:35,140
Quick. Speak up.

396
00:17:36,830 --> 00:17:37,900
I know a way

397
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:40,420
to let you see what this man looks like.

398
00:17:42,010 --> 00:17:42,680
How?

399
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:45,220
By making the Yellow Immortal

400
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:46,480
take a picture of him?

401
00:17:47,110 --> 00:17:48,200
You want to see his face or not?

402
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,440
Speak your mind already.
